  "question": {
    "text": "The quadratic equations <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> have one root in common. The other roots of the first equation and the second equation are integers in the ratio <math><mn>4</mn><mi></mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the common root is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>α</mi></math> be the common root and the other roots of the equations be <math><mn>4</mn><mi>β</mi></math> and <math><mn>3</mn><mi>β</mi></math> respectively. Then,<br /><math><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>α</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>α</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br />The first equation is <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Whose roots are <math><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mn>4</mn></math><br />If <math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />So, roots of first equation is <math><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>4</mn></math> and that of second equation is <math><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>3</mn></math><br />If <math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>3</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>4</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />Here the roots are not integers <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>"
  }
}